INT. ABANDONED BOWLING ALLEY - NIGHT

Dead neon. Lane 6 still has pins. A birthday banner droops: HAPPY 40TH, KEVIN.

DOT, forties, event planner, clipboard clamped to her chest, shoves a cake onto the ball return while FITZ, thirties, in a rented shark costume, trips over his own fin and takes down a rack of house shoes and OGUNLEYE, "GUNNY" to all, sixties, a retired lane mechanic with a toolbox, drops to one knee to catch the cake before it slides off, and the ball return rumbles, and the cake shoots down Lane 6 like a torpedo.

Silence. A single pin wobbles.

DOT
Nobody saw that.

FITZ
(muffled, in the shark head)
I saw it. I'm a shark. We see everything.

GUNNY
That cake had eighty dollars of fondant on it.

DOT
Kevin arrives in ten minutes. Ten.

Fitz yanks the shark head off, sweaty, hair plastered.

FITZ
I can't breathe in this thing. Why am I a shark?

DOT
Kevin loves sharks.

FITZ
Kevin loves SHARKS. Not men inside sharks.

Gunny walks down the lane, picks up the ruined cake with both hands like an infant, and carries it back, frosting to the elbows.

GUNNY
I can fix it. Give me a spatula and a prayer.

DOT
I have neither. I have a clipboard.

An INTERCOM crackles overhead.

PRU (V.O.)
(over intercom, bored)
Attention, party in Lane 6. Your guest of honor is in the parking lot and he's on the phone with his mother.

DOT
How long?

PRU (V.O.)
His mother is Greek. I'd say forty minutes.

Dot exhales for the first time in an hour. She sits on the ball return.

FITZ
So we have time.

DOT
We have time.

GUNNY
(scraping frosting)
Then somebody hand me a spatula.

Fitz offers a bowling shoe. Gunny takes it, considers it, and uses it.

PRU (V.O.)
(over intercom)
For the record, the shark is good.

Fitz bows. His fin knocks over the last pin.
